\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid11954050 The Paris Branch of The Royal British Legion, jointly with our partners M\'e9moire et Espoirs de la R\'e9
sistance, have arranged a Franco-British evening  at the Ambassador\rquote s Residence, 39, rue du Faubourg St Honor\'e9;
\par 
\par Guest speakers will talk in French from their personal experience of Franco-British cooperation during the Second World War in support of the R\'e9
sistance movement.  They will therefore touch inter alia on the relationship between Sir Winston Churchill and G\'e9n\'e9ral Charles de Gaulle.
\par 
\par The speakers are:  
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid11954050 Madame Noreen Riols
\par }{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid11954050 Former member of staff at S.O.E. in Colonel Buckmaster\rquote s office. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\insrsid11954050\charrsid11954050 Monsieur Jean-Louis Cr\'e9mieux-Brilhac, CBE
\par }{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid11954050 Historian, former member of  F.F.L, and author of  \'ab\~La France Libre T2\~\'bb
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\insrsid11954050\charrsid11954050 Dr Pierre Morel  KMC
\par }{\fs24\insrsid11954050\charrsid11954050 Pr\'e9sident de la F\'e9d\'e9ration Nationale de }{\fs24\insrsid6299026 Libre R\'e9sistance, Officier Liqui}{\fs24\insrsid11954050\charrsid11954050 dateur du R\'e9seau Oscar Buckmaster
\par 
